65
00:03:53,199 --> 00:03:54,000
(Correct)
(One.)

66
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:58,599
(So you haven't forgotten it.)

67
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:01,960
(July 15, 2015)

68
00:04:01,960 --> 00:04:04,080
(was your daughter
Zhang Xiaoya's birthday)

69
00:04:04,879 --> 00:04:05,960
(and the day she died.)

70
00:04:05,960 --> 00:04:06,599
(Dad,)

71
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:09,439
(you're a great hero,)

72
00:04:09,439 --> 00:04:11,199
(a great charity donor,)

73
00:04:11,439 --> 00:04:13,479
(and the person I admired most!)

74
00:04:19,759 --> 00:04:21,839
You're nothing but a hypocrite.

75
00:04:21,839 --> 00:04:22,759
You're the devil.

76
00:04:22,759 --> 00:04:23,800
You're a demon!

77
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:15,720
(Serve with Loyalty and Innovation)
She got here at dawn.

78
00:06:15,759 --> 00:06:17,360
She's been keeping us up all night.

79
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:18,560
She refuses to go home,

80
00:06:18,839 --> 00:06:20,519
saying a female ghost is after her.

81
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:22,360
By the way, she said she's Xu Meng.

82
00:06:22,839 --> 00:06:23,639
Xu Meng?

83
00:06:23,879 --> 00:06:25,800
We've been looking for her for ages.

84
00:06:28,879 --> 00:06:29,920
Any history of drug use?

85
00:06:30,319 --> 00:06:31,120
We tested her.

86
00:06:31,279 --> 00:06:32,079
Negative.

87
00:06:34,639 --> 00:06:36,079
Her eye whites are bloodshot,

88
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:37,480
and her dark circles are severe.

89
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:39,560
She's been suffering
from long-term sleep problems.

90
00:06:39,959 --> 00:06:41,399
Her frown lines are pronounced,

91
00:06:41,839 --> 00:06:43,079
and her lips are very dry.

92
00:06:43,439 --> 00:06:44,879
She's clearly anxious.

93
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:46,759
Based on all these signs,

94
00:06:46,759 --> 00:06:48,360
she's likely been suffering

95
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:49,879
from a sleep disorder
for three to six months.

96
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:51,720
Let's go in and ask her.

97
00:06:51,959 --> 00:06:52,759
Come on, Ziyan.

98
00:07:07,519 --> 00:07:09,120
We're with
the Longfan Criminal Investigation Team.

99
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:10,079
I'm Han Liang.

100
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:12,759
What are you afraid of?

101
00:07:12,759 --> 00:07:14,959
Tell us. Maybe we can help.

102
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:18,319
A... a voice.

103
00:07:19,959 --> 00:07:22,120
It sounds like a girl crying.

104
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:23,519
No, humming a song.

105
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:26,319
Xu Meng,

106
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:28,120
tell us.

107
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:29,360
What kind of girl was she?

108
00:07:30,360 --> 00:07:31,759
Do you recognize the voice?

109
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:52,560
It's... it's Zhang Xiaoya.

110
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:53,560
It has to be her.

111
00:07:54,959 --> 00:07:56,959
Yes. That's exactly who I saw!

112
00:07:57,839 --> 00:07:59,519
She's come back for me.

113
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:01,000
Zhang Xiaoya?

114
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:02,480
What did you do to her?

115
00:08:07,439 --> 00:08:08,920
Our records show

116
00:08:09,319 --> 00:08:10,480
you were an early beneficiary

117
00:08:10,759 --> 00:08:12,720
of Zhang Xiaodong's charity fund.

118
00:08:13,439 --> 00:08:15,639
So, what do you remember

119
00:08:15,639 --> 00:08:17,519
about Mr. Zhang or his family?

120
00:08:17,680 --> 00:08:19,279
Say, his daughter,

121
00:08:19,319 --> 00:08:20,800
Zhang Xiaoya?

122
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:23,199
Nothing.

123
00:08:24,279 --> 00:08:25,519
Just a regular sponsorship.

124
00:08:25,879 --> 00:08:27,360
I barely ever saw them.

125
00:08:27,879 --> 00:08:28,800
If you weren't close,

126
00:08:28,959 --> 00:08:30,680
why would you be afraid?

127
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:33,519
Unless your time with her

128
00:08:33,919 --> 00:08:35,360
or what happened to her

129
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:37,360
was far more serious.

130
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:40,720
Have you been to Fengshan Villa

131
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:42,360
for Zhang Xiaoya's birthday before?

132
00:08:44,639 --> 00:08:45,440
Xu Meng.

133
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:47,759
Tell me.

134
00:08:47,759 --> 00:08:49,720
What exactly happened at Fengshan Villa

135
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:51,320
ten years ago?

136
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:54,120
What happened that night,

137
00:08:54,840 --> 00:08:55,919
on her birthday?

138
00:09:08,879 --> 00:09:09,679
Meng.

139
00:09:10,639 --> 00:09:11,519
Where's Xiaoxue?

140
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:14,480
Why wasn't she there for the cake?

141
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:16,759
Is she still feeling sick?

142
00:09:17,559 --> 00:09:18,759
I should go check on her.

143
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:25,399
What's wrong, Meng?

144
00:09:26,480 --> 00:09:27,919
Why are you crying?

145
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:31,279
Let's go find her together, okay?

146
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:34,759
What's wrong?

147
00:09:36,639 --> 00:09:37,440
Xiaoya,

148
00:09:38,159 --> 00:09:39,679
are we besties?

149
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:41,600
Of course we are.

150
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:44,960
You, me, and Xiaoxue.

151
00:09:45,679 --> 00:09:47,279
The three of us.

152
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:49,279
Didn't we promise

153
00:09:49,639 --> 00:09:51,480
to be besties for life?

154
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:54,120
Meng.

155
00:09:54,759 --> 00:09:56,200
Don't cry.

156
00:09:58,080 --> 00:09:58,879
What's wrong?

157
00:09:59,440 --> 00:10:01,120
Tell me what happened.

158
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:01,840
Okay?

159
00:10:02,679 --> 00:10:03,480
Okay?

160
00:10:16,559 --> 00:10:17,679
Where did Zhang Xiaoya go?

161
00:10:17,799 --> 00:10:19,440
Did she go to question her father?

162
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:23,879
That night at Fengshan Villa,

163
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:25,200
you were the last one,

164
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:26,679
or one of the few,

165
00:10:26,840 --> 00:10:29,320
to know Zhang Xiaoya went to her father.

166
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,519
And then something happened to her,

167
00:10:31,519 --> 00:10:32,279
right?

168
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:45,799
How did you become friends
with Zhang Xiaoya?

169
00:10:55,279 --> 00:10:56,600
(Debt Offset Service Agreement)
Sign the contracts.

170
00:10:57,159 --> 00:10:59,480
I'll keep my promise to you.

171
00:10:59,639 --> 00:11:00,879
But keep this confidential.

172
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:06,039
Ms. Su!

173
00:11:08,840 --> 00:11:09,639
Xiaoya?

174
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:11,919
Why are you back?

175
00:11:11,919 --> 00:11:14,039
Weren't you taking IELTS classes?

176
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:16,279
It was so boring,

177
00:11:16,279 --> 00:11:17,480
so I snuck back.

178
00:11:17,799 --> 00:11:18,519
Ms. Su,

179
00:11:19,279 --> 00:11:20,840
please don't tell my dad.

180
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:21,840
Please.

181
00:11:21,879 --> 00:11:23,080
You're the best!

182
00:11:23,399 --> 00:11:24,200
All right.

183
00:11:26,559 --> 00:11:27,440
Who are they?

184
00:11:29,039 --> 00:11:29,840
Them?

185
00:11:30,240 --> 00:11:32,000
They're students your father sponsors.

186
00:11:33,080 --> 00:11:33,879
Hi.

187
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,039
I'm Zhang Xiaoya.

188
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:43,200
Hi. I'm Xiaoxue.

189
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:45,639
Just call me Meng.

190
00:11:48,399 --> 00:11:49,799
What are you doing?

191
00:11:50,879 --> 00:11:52,120
I hate that my dad drinks.

192
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:54,480
When he gets drunk,

193
00:11:54,480 --> 00:11:56,039
he has even less time for me.

194
00:11:56,279 --> 00:11:58,480
He's barely home.

195
00:11:58,559 --> 00:12:00,200
When he is, he just stays in his room.

196
00:12:00,879 --> 00:12:02,039
Let me pour them all out.

197
00:12:03,399 --> 00:12:04,279
Oh my God!

198
00:12:04,679 --> 00:12:06,240
This bottle costs thousands of euros!

199
00:12:06,480 --> 00:12:07,639
Who cares?

200
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:13,480
Come on. Help me pour them all.

201
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:25,879
You know what?

202
00:12:26,279 --> 00:12:27,639
My dad secretly keeps

203
00:12:27,639 --> 00:12:29,440
a bunch of crocodiles in the pool.

204
00:12:29,879 --> 00:12:31,240
Let's see if they get drunk

205
00:12:31,279 --> 00:12:33,240
and come charging at us.

206
00:12:41,559 --> 00:12:42,600
It's pretty good.

207
00:12:43,480 --> 00:12:44,279
Let me try it.

208
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:49,399
Have some.

209
00:12:49,559 --> 00:12:50,360
It tastes good!

210
00:12:53,159 --> 00:12:53,960
Drink up.

211
00:13:11,679 --> 00:13:13,600
Do crocodiles really eat people?

212
00:13:14,039 --> 00:13:15,679
I don't know if crocodiles eat people,

213
00:13:16,039 --> 00:13:17,200
but I'll eat you first.

214
00:13:22,279 --> 00:13:24,799
Three, two, one!

215
00:13:36,919 --> 00:13:39,440
Xiaoya was a kind and innocent girl.

216
00:13:39,639 --> 00:13:41,559
After discovering
something so horrifying,

217
00:13:41,559 --> 00:13:42,759
would she just let it go?

218
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:46,159
What could she have said to her father?

219
00:13:46,519 --> 00:13:47,320
An argument?

220
00:13:47,759 --> 00:13:48,559
A confrontation?

221
00:13:48,919 --> 00:13:49,960
Where were you

222
00:13:50,360 --> 00:13:51,399
at the time?

223
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:54,360
Were you right there with her?

224
00:13:56,399 --> 00:13:57,240
I...

225
00:13:58,120 --> 00:13:59,840
I just wanted to follow her.

226
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:01,480
I was afraid she'd...

227
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:02,759
Afraid of what?

228
00:14:03,039 --> 00:14:03,879
That something might happen to her?

229
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:05,679
So what did you see?

230
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:17,480
It... it was Zhang Xiaodong.

231
00:14:19,399 --> 00:14:20,279
What's wrong?

232
00:14:21,399 --> 00:14:23,679
Who upset my little princess?

233
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:29,960
Tell me.

234
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:31,279
What did you do to Xiaoxue?

235
00:14:37,320 --> 00:14:38,120
Xiaoya,

236
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,480
some things are complicated.

237
00:14:41,159 --> 00:14:42,360
It's not what you think.

238
00:14:43,799 --> 00:14:45,120
I'm disgusted.

239
00:14:45,399 --> 00:14:47,159
This family, and you,

240
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:48,639
all disgust me!

241
00:14:48,639 --> 00:14:49,399
Enough!

242
00:14:49,759 --> 00:14:51,639
You shouldn't ask about this.

243
00:14:52,919 --> 00:14:53,840
Go back to your room.

244
00:14:54,559 --> 00:14:55,840
I always thought

245
00:14:56,840 --> 00:14:58,600
you were the person I admired most.

246
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:00,240
I always thought

247
00:15:00,240 --> 00:15:02,879
you were a great charity donor!

248
00:15:04,440 --> 00:15:05,840
Did you...

249
00:15:06,360 --> 00:15:07,840
- Did you...
- Shut up!

250
00:15:08,159 --> 00:15:09,600
What do you know?

251
00:15:12,840 --> 00:15:14,600
To build this whole business,

252
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:17,240
I need to entertain people
and grease some palms.

253
00:15:17,559 --> 00:15:19,039
They get financial support,

254
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:20,759
so they owe me something in return.

255
00:15:20,799 --> 00:15:22,200
That's only fair.

256
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:24,399
Without me, they're nothing!

257
00:15:24,399 --> 00:15:26,559
- Nothing!
- I'm calling the police.

258
00:15:26,559 --> 00:15:27,679
I'll tell everyone

259
00:15:27,679 --> 00:15:28,759
- what kind of person you are!
- You dare!

260
00:15:28,759 --> 00:15:29,559
Get back here!

261
00:15:29,559 --> 00:15:30,200
Let go of me!

262
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:31,919
Xiaoya, have you lost your mind?

263
00:15:31,919 --> 00:15:33,799
- You're a wolf in sheep's clothing.
- Zhang Xiaoya...

264
00:15:33,799 --> 00:15:35,039
You're a hypocrite!

265
00:15:35,039 --> 00:15:35,840
Xiaoya!

266
00:15:36,759 --> 00:15:37,799
Please, honey.

267
00:15:38,320 --> 00:15:39,679
Don't call the police.

268
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,759
If you do, we're all finished.

269
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:42,639
Please?

270
00:15:43,039 --> 00:15:44,039
I did all this

271
00:15:44,240 --> 00:15:45,279
for you,

272
00:15:45,399 --> 00:15:46,120
for this family.

273
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:46,960
For me?

274
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:48,360
Or for yourself?

275
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:49,559
- You know the answer!
- It was all for you!

276
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:51,279
It had nothing to do with me!

277
00:15:51,559 --> 00:15:53,600
- Can't you stop being so stubborn?
- You did it for yourself!

278
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:56,159
Can't you listen to me for once?

279
00:15:57,080 --> 00:15:59,799
Can't you try to understand me?

280
00:16:13,960 --> 00:16:15,200
Zhang Xiaoya had an accident.

281
00:16:15,360 --> 00:16:16,360
What about Xiaoxue?

282
00:16:16,799 --> 00:16:18,240
Did she know about that?

283
00:16:18,799 --> 00:16:19,639
Where did she go?

284
00:16:20,440 --> 00:16:21,240
I...

285
00:16:22,360 --> 00:16:24,000
I never saw her again.

286
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:24,720
Xu Meng,

287
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:26,240
think carefully before you answer me.

288
00:16:26,240 --> 00:16:28,000
I really haven't seen her again.

289
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:31,360
Then do you know He Guifen is dead?

290
00:16:31,440 --> 00:16:32,399
I know!

291
00:16:33,159 --> 00:16:34,039
She deserved it.

292
00:16:35,159 --> 00:16:36,000
She's the one

293
00:16:36,159 --> 00:16:38,000
who pushed me into hell!

294
00:16:38,240 --> 00:16:39,399
It was all for money.

295
00:16:39,840 --> 00:16:41,000
She deserved to be scammed!

296
00:16:42,399 --> 00:16:43,840
She was murdered.

297
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:47,440
Xu Meng,

298
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,480
someone's avenging your past.

299
00:16:50,919 --> 00:16:51,840
Do you know that?

300
00:16:59,240 --> 00:17:00,320
(I will gather evidence)

301
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:03,279
(and make them pay.)

302
00:17:06,160 --> 00:17:07,799
(Later I fled Longfan)

303
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:09,559
(and never contacted her again.)

304
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:11,440
(But one day...)

305
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:41,359
What was the evidence

306
00:17:41,359 --> 00:17:42,359
she talked about?

307
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:43,960
I don't know.

308
00:17:45,240 --> 00:17:47,240
Xiaoxue had a USB drive.

309
00:17:47,839 --> 00:17:49,440
She always kept it on her.

310
00:17:49,519 --> 00:17:50,599
What was on the USB drive?

311
00:17:52,799 --> 00:17:53,799
I didn't dare ask.

312
00:17:54,759 --> 00:17:56,839
I didn't even dare think about it.

313
00:17:57,319 --> 00:17:59,119
I just wanted to pretend

314
00:17:59,119 --> 00:18:00,839
that time never happened.

315
00:18:04,240 --> 00:18:05,000
Xiaoxue?

316
00:18:08,440 --> 00:18:09,279
Xiaoxue...

317
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:40,753
♪Sunset washes over the old wall♪

318
00:18:41,310 --> 00:18:45,460
♪Milk tea cools on the stone steps♪

319
00:18:45,633 --> 00:18:49,310
♪Sea wind tugs at your sleeve♪

320
00:18:49,980 --> 00:18:53,886
♪Unspoken words just flee and fade♪

321
00:19:02,926 --> 00:19:06,600
♪The marks on the desk
have faded yellow♪

322
00:19:06,940 --> 00:19:09,320
♪I turned around,
and a gunshot rang out♪

323
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:14,060
♪No one can truly feel another's pain♪

324
00:19:14,126 --> 00:19:17,880
♪The wind is cold,
a fading shadow sways♪

325
00:19:18,206 --> 00:19:22,480
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

326
00:19:22,900 --> 00:19:26,860
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

327
00:19:27,953 --> 00:19:31,140
♪A bullet pierces the spring night♪

328
00:19:31,913 --> 00:19:35,800
♪You sink into the vast crowd♪

329
00:19:44,790 --> 00:19:48,580
♪Years later, when we meet again♪

330
00:19:48,993 --> 00:19:52,870
♪Don't mention this moonlit night♪

331
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:56,780
♪The waves smooth
two lines of footprints♪

332
00:19:56,940 --> 00:19:59,790
♪Half a cup of sweetness
sinks into the sand♪

333
00:19:59,846 --> 00:20:04,510
♪Tonight, I don't care
about the universe♪

334
00:20:04,780 --> 00:20:08,860
♪I only want to see this through
with you♪

335
00:20:09,440 --> 00:20:11,630
♪Wind back to shore,
clouds back to hills♪

336
00:20:11,686 --> 00:20:13,430
♪We stop here in this night♪

337
00:20:13,726 --> 00:20:18,120
♪This is the past, the only,
the last look back♪

338
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:23,913
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

339
00:20:26,766 --> 00:20:32,440
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

340
00:20:44,353 --> 00:20:47,270
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

341
00:20:47,270 --> 00:20:51,846
♪One gunshot echoes through half a life♪

342
